{"id": "EUVD-2026-77008", "enisaUuid": "dd4550cd-d5f4-3578-85ce-59aef94fb6f1", "description": "alsa-lib through 1.2.16.1 contains a stack buffer overflow in the __snd_ctl_ascii_elem_id_parse() function that writes one byte past a 64-byte buffer when parsing a name= field with 64 or more characters. Attackers can supply a long control-element identifier string through saved state files or command-line arguments to overwrite adjacent stack memory and crash the calling process.", "datePublished": "2026-09-13T12:22:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-16T14:07:43", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/alsa-project/alsa-lib/commit/f84cd4ced7b36fddb8e4ee24404cf7c091d27020", "https://github.com/alsa-project/alsa-lib/blob/v1.2.16.1/src/control/ctlparse.c#L216-L241", "https://lore.kernel.org/alsa-devel/CACBQ=P2FhO3M6dkv3cWuKb6Qhs92ouV+FJ3SJZ_PVBSSdJWRAQ@mail.gmail.com/", "https://github.com/alsa-project/alsa-lib", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/alsa-lib-through-1.2.16.1-off-by-one-stack-buffer-overflow-in-snd-ctl-ascii-elem-id-parse"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90781", "GHSA-f8w2-9vv9-pxwq"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "66b10597-ea31-335f-bc76-bf3a4d431d84", "product": {"name": "alsa-lib", "vendor": {"name": "ALSA Project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.16.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c8e5c402-ebd5-35b5-8909-6a96f359c8aa", "vendor": {"name": "ALSA Project"}}], "isExploited": false}